      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Reps should acknowledge the data directly by stating, \"Yes, our clinical trials show a 5% higher rate of mild dizziness compared to Zenitrol,\" to build immediate credibility. They should then reframe the perspective by explaining that this is a transient issue for 10% of patients that is typically resolved quickly with dose titration, whereas Zenitrol may offer other trade-offs we haven't discussed yet. Finally, they should pivot to the bigger picture: \"Ultimately, while mild dizziness is a consideration, our overall safety profile and superior efficacy in your target patient population make CardioZen the stronger choice for long-term adherence and outcomes.\"",
      "source": "target",
